From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Wed, 17 Sep 2026 15:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: the screen sharing picker, the edge and the Stop pill

When an application asks to share the screen, the ScreenCast portal showed
GNOME's "Share Screen" dialog: a list of window names with nothing to look
at. Luma shows Share instead -- the requesting application on the card's
axis, a plain title, a Windows / Screens switch over live previews of every
window and screen, a few clear options, and equal Cancel and Share buttons.
While sharing, what is shared wears a violet edge and a pill above the shelf
holds Stop.

The card is drawn by the Shell because the previews are live window content
and the card is modal over the session, neither of which a GTK portal process
can do; luma-portal implements the ScreenCast backend and asks the Shell over
one private interface. ADR-041 records the decision and the measured cost of
the alternative.

The picker (lumaShare.js, luma-share.css):
- The authentication prompt's card language: the same scrim, 24 radius, Quick
  Options tokens, 17px/750 title, 13.5px muted body and equal button pair,
  600 wide, scrolling inside itself when it is taller than the screen.
- The requester's 56 icon with a 26 violet screen badge overlapping its lower
  right corner by 7, ringed 3 in the card; a neutral system screen when the
  requester cannot be resolved. The name and icon come from the system, never
  from text the application supplied, and a site is named only when the
  request carries a trusted origin.
- A Windows / Screens segmented control, hidden when the request allows one
  type. Previews are 16:10 tiles, 3 columns for windows and 2 for screens,
  with the source at 92% of its tile so its own corners and shadow show, an
  18 app icon, the window title and the application's name or the monitor's
  resolution. Hover, focus and a 2.5 violet chosen ring, with a 22 violet
  check badge.
- A window preview is the dock's live preview renderer (0117), now exported
  rather than copied: a clone of the window actor already in the scene graph,
  painted at thumbnail size. A screen preview clones the window group -- the
  wallpaper and every window, and no Shell chrome -- so a preview can never
  contain the picker drawing itself.
- Show pointer maps to the portal's cursor mode; Hide notifications while
  sharing reads Luma Cast's own silence-notifications key, so the two never
  disagree. Let <app> control this computer appears only for a RemoteDesktop
  request that asked for keyboard or pointer.
- Keyboard: focus starts on the first preview, arrows move the choice, Space
  selects, Enter shares, Escape cancels. With the pointer, a second click on
  the chosen preview shares it, so a double-click shares; this uses no
  button-press handler, which would stop firing silently once St.Button
  handles clicks as gestures. With several sources allowed a second click
  deselects instead. Previews are radio
  buttons, or checkboxes when the request allows several sources, named
  "<app>, <window>"; the tabs are a tab list and the options are switches
  with their own descriptions.

While sharing:
- A shared window wears a 2.5 violet ring with a 7 halo that follows it; a
  shared monitor gets a 3 inset violet edge. Both are CaptureHidden actors
  whose violet is drawn by a child, so they are on the screen and never in
  the stream: Clutter paints an actor's own node (where St draws its
  background and border) before paint(), which is all CaptureHidden
  overrides, so an edge styled on the outer actor went into every screen
  stream. The screen edge takes no input, so the shared screen stays usable.
- A 40 pill in the shelf surface slot, placed by the one shelf placement
  helper, names what is shared and with whom and holds Stop. Stop ends every
  stream for the session and tells the backend to close it.
- Banners wait and arrive once sharing stops. Casting drops what it silences,
  because a receiver may be left running for hours; a share is a conversation
  that ends, and what waited is still worth seeing.
- The Well's sharing mark stands down while the pill is up, so the same thing
  is not said twice. Other kinds of remote access keep it.

The owner's three open questions are not answered yet. Each interim answer is
one constant at the top of lumaShare.js: the pill replaces the Well's mark,
the pill stays for the whole share, and there is no "choose on screen" mode.

The picker's card carries the Shell ink ledger (0150) itself, because its
stylesheet is created here: frost is the smoked veil rgba(28,33,40,0.88) and
glass rgba(14,19,26,0.82), both with white ink, and the Share button and the
Stop pill keep their light plate on hover on both smoked treatments. Without
that last part the unqualified :hover laid #3d4249 under the plate's dark
label, which 0150's verify-treatment-ink.py fails at %build. The selected
tab, the tab hover and the pill's own surface also name their ink on frost,
where they had inherited the light card's dark ink from an unqualified rule.

Reuse rather than a second copy: lumaCapture's shelf surface takes a style
prefix, the dock's preview thumbnail is exported, and reading the monitors'
names moves out of Luma Cast's manager into one listDisplays().
